menu "Preamp knob remote"

config KNOB_WIFI_SSID
    string "Home WiFi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Used only to fetch the album cover.  Control runs over ESP-NOW
        and works with this left empty - you just get no artwork.

config KNOB_WIFI_PASS
    string "Home WiFi password"
    default ""

config KNOB_FALLBACK_CHANNEL
    int "Fallback ESP-NOW channel"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    help
        Used on the very first wake, before the knob has ever
        associated and cached the real channel.  Must match
        AMP_ESPNOW_CHANNEL on the amplifier's C3.

config KNOB_PI_BASE_URL
    string "Base URL for the cover endpoint on the Pi"
    default "http://moode.local/amp"
    help
        The knob GETs <base>/cover.jpg?id=N and expects a 480x480
        baseline JPEG.  Scaling happens on the Pi: it has the CPU, and
        an arbitrary-size cover would need a second full-screen buffer
        plus a resampler on this chip.

endmenu
